<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Code Noir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1685">1685</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Code Noir was a decree issued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> in 1685 to regulate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the French colonies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. It defined enslaved people as property, set harsh punishments, required Catholic baptism and restricted freedom for the enslaved. A revised version was issued for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> in 1724, and it remained in force until slavery was abolished.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/code-noir.jpg" alt="Code Noir" width="320" height="646" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: France, Louis XV, Prault pere · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Code_Noir_1742_edition.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
